       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, GI bleeding and hyponatremia. They haven't been shown to work better. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **Sertraline 200 mg PO daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **Sertraline 50 mg PO daily**, the usual starting dose for depression. For depression, the dose is typically titrated in 25\u201350 mg steps at least a week apart.\n- **A different dose**, if you were thinking of a specific indication or a titration plan.\n\nIf you really do want 400 mg, for example on a specialist's recommendation, tell me and I'll enter it. I'd add a note with the rationale. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it too.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
